# .easignore — what EAS Build uploads.
#
# EAS archives from the GIT ROOT, not from eddy-ios/. That is deliberate and
# load-bearing: metro.config.js watches ../packages and
# ../missouri-float-planner/shared, so an archive scoped to the app directory
# fails before bundling even starts ("ENOENT ... /packages" out of Metro's
# verifyRootExists). Do not try to "fix" that by scoping the archive down.
#
# But archiving the whole repo means uploading 84 MB of Remotion audio, blog
# imagery and marketing PDFs on every build, none of which the app bundle
# touches. So this file is an ALLOWLIST: deny everything, then re-admit only
# what Metro actually resolves.
#
# ── The trap ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# When .easignore exists, eas-cli STOPS READING .gitignore ENTIRELY
# (eas-cli/build/vcs/local.js: "if .easignore exists, .gitignore files are not
# used"). Every gitignored path is therefore uploaded unless it is re-stated
# here — including .env files. Writing this as an allowlist rather than a
# denylist is what makes that safe by construction: secrets are excluded
# because nothing is admitted unless it is named.
#
# Only .git and node_modules are ignored unconditionally by eas-cli itself.
#
# Verify after any edit:  python3 eddy-ios/scripts/check-easignore.py

# Deny everything at the root.
/*

# The app itself.
!/eddy-ios

# Shared TypeScript resolved by metro.config.js watchFolders + tsconfig paths:
#   @eddy/types, @eddy/geo, @eddy/offline, @eddy/sync, @eddy/hazards
!/packages

# @shared/* — the canonical condition system. Re-admit the parent directory,
# then deny its contents, then re-admit only shared/. Gitignore cannot
# re-include a path whose parent directory is excluded, so the walk down has to
# be explicit at every level.
!/missouri-float-planner
/missouri-float-planner/*
!/missouri-float-planner/shared

# Build output and local secrets. Re-stated because .gitignore is not consulted
# once this file exists — see the trap above.
.env
.env.*
.expo/
dist/
